Exercise 8: CloudWatch Monitoring for EC2 Instances

This exercise demonstrates how to monitor an Amazon EC2 instance using AWS CloudWatch and configure alarms to trigger notifications when specific performance thresholds are exceeded.  
It was completed as part of my Cloud Architecture Practicals in the 5th semester of BCA (Cloud Computing) at Kristu Jayanti College.


   Objective
To understand how to:
- Monitor EC2 instance metrics using AWS CloudWatch
- Enable detailed monitoring
- Create CloudWatch alarms for CPU utilization
- Receive notifications when thresholds are crossed


 Steps Performed

  1.Enable Detailed Monitoring
- Logged in to AWS Management Console
- Navigated to EC2 → Instances
- Selected the EC2 instance
- Enabled Detailed Monitoring (1-minute intervals)


  2.Open CloudWatch Console
- Navigated to AWS CloudWatch
- Selected Alarms → Create alarm


  3.Configure CPU Utilization Alarm
- Selected EC2 Metrics → Per-Instance Metrics
- Chose CPUUtilization
- Set condition:
  - Threshold: CPU utilization > 30%

   4.Configure Notification
- Selected In Alarm state
- Chose an existing SNS topic or created a new one
- Subscribed email address and confirmed subscription

   5.Create Alarm
- Gave alarm name (e.g., `HighCPUAlarm`)
- Reviewed configuration
- Created the alarm

  6. Verify Alarm
- Alarm initially in OK state
- When CPU usage exceeded threshold:
  - Alarm changed to In Alarm
  - Email notification sent via SNS.

## ✅ Result
CloudWatch successfully monitored EC2 performance and triggered an alarm when CPU utilization crossed the defined threshold. Email notification was received confirming alarm activation.
